<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cornelius Vanderbilt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1794–1877</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cornelius Vanderbilt was an American shipping and railway <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a>, one of the richest men of the nineteenth century. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> Gold Rush his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accessory-transit-company">Accessory Transit Company</a> carried travellers between the Atlantic and Pacific across Nicaragua from 1851, and in 1856–1857 he helped the Central American states drive out the filibuster <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-walker">William Walker</a> after Walker seized the company's property. He later built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Central Railroad.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cornelius-vanderbilt.jpg" alt="Cornelius Vanderbilt" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Produced by Mathew Brady's studio, restored by Michel Vuijlsteke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cornelius_Vanderbilt_Daguerrotype2_(cropped)(b).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
